{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"putrid-uncheered-blueshark","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# S1 — extract the retry/error cluster out of `transport.py` (behaviour-preserving)\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nSplit out of [rebar:b586-2fda-8a15-4260], whose plan hit BLOCK ten times. The round-by-round\nrecord is on that ticket; the structural finding is that it carried TWO independent changes — a\nmechanical relocation and a new 429 policy — and every round found new surface because a fix to\none re-opened the other. Rounds 6-7 were about THIS half's mechanics; rounds 1, 4, 8, 9, 10 were\nabout the policy half (now S2). Splitting is the same move that turned J9's eight BLOCKs into a\nfirst-try PASS as J10.\n\nThis story is the mechanical half and is **forced by the module-size cap, not by taste**:\n`transport.py` is **789 lines on `origin/main`** against the LOCKED 800-line cap\n(`.github/module-size-limit.txt`), so there are ELEVEN lines of headroom and the 429 policy cannot\nbe added in place. (Recording the measurement because this file's LOC has been misquoted twice in\nepic e369: the earlier \"792 vs 789\" disagreement was a pre-/post-9263 base difference, and now\nthat 9263 is merged both readings agree at 789.)\n\n## Approach\n\n**Relocate, do not redesign.** Move the retry/error cluster from\n`adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py` into a new `adapters/jira_datacenter/retry.py`, changing\nno behaviour. The cluster is `_connection_retry_exceptions`, `_jira_http_error_types`,\n`_as_backend_http_error`, `TlsVerificationError`, `_tls_verification_error`, and\n`_with_connection_retry`.\n\n**`TlsVerificationError` MUST move with the rest.** `_tls_verification_error` returns it, so\nleaving the class behind in `transport.py` makes `retry.py` import from `transport.py` while\n`transport.py` imports `_with_connection_retry` from `retry.py` — a circular import. The class and\nits factory are one unit.\n\n**Re-export from `transport.py` so existing importers keep working.** `test_jira_dc_config_settings.py`\nimports `TlsVerificationError` from the transport module; that test must pass UNEDITED, because\nediting it to chase the move would convert a regression signal into a rubber stamp.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/retry.py` — NEW; the moved cluster.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py` — cluster deleted,\n  cluster imported, names re-exported.\n\n**NOT in scope:** any behaviour change, and specifically any 429 / `Retry-After` handling — that is\nS2. If this story changes what any call does, it has failed.\n\n## Testing\n\nThe oracle for a pure relocation is that the EXISTING suite passes unedited — a new test asserting\nthe code moved would only restate the diff.\n\n* `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` DC transport tests pass with NO edits.\n* `test_jira_dc_config_settings.py` passes with NO edits (proves the re-export works).\n* The module-size gate passes, and `transport.py` is measurably smaller.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `retry.py` exists and contains all six named members, and `transport.py` no longer defines\n      them\n- [ ] `TlsVerificationError` lives in `retry.py` WITH `_tls_verification_error`, and a test or a\n      clean `python -c \"import ...\"` proves there is no circular import between the two modules\n- [ ] `transport.py` re-exports the moved names, and `test_jira_dc_config_settings.py` passes\n      **with zero edits to that file** — asserted by `git diff --exit-code` on it\n- [ ] the full DC transport unit suite passes with zero test edits; if any test needed an edit,\n      this story is not behaviour-preserving and must be reworked rather than the test adjusted\n- [ ] `transport.py` is under the 800-line cap with headroom for S2, and the measured before/after\n      line counts are recorded on this ticket\n- [ ] NO diff hunk changes control flow, retry counts, backoff values, or exception types — a\n      reviewer can confirm the change is a move by reading the diff alone","id":"f2f3-9cb1-335b-4e31","parent_id":"b586-2fda-8a15-4260","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"S1 — extract the retry/error cluster out of transport.py (behaviour-preserving)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785615599519232001,"uuid":"a7bf4fb9-d49a-4f8f-a040-e5e1c3ec9fc8"}